---
import Exit from './Exit.astro';
import { narration } from '../narrative';

const act = narration.actOne;
---

<!--
  ACT II — the vocabulary is yours. §9.2.

  A STATIC BLOCK, and deliberately: §9.7 budgets every animated scene four times over
  (desktop, mobile, reduced motion, no script) and fixes the order in which that cost is
  given back — merge two scenes, merge the hinge with what follows, then downgrade a whole
  act. Act one is never downgraded, because it alone carries the demonstration. This is that
  order applied rather than a corner cut.
-->
<section class="act" id="act-two" aria-labelledby="act-two-heading">
    <div class="shell">
        <p class="act-mark">Act two</p>
        <h2 id="act-two-heading">The words are yours</h2>

        <div class="prose">
            <p>
                A theme is a JSON file. No code, no recompiling, no plugin: a list of nouns, the
                adjectives and participles that may stand in front of them, and the categories
                that say which meets which.
            </p>
            <p>
                <strong>It is known by its file name.</strong> Drop
                <code class="mono">{act.theme}.json</code> in the theme directory and ask for
                <code class="mono">{act.theme}</code>. A file named after a theme the engine
                carries shadows it — allowed, and announced.
            </p>
            <p>
                Ask for several at once and the draw is weighted across them, each theme staying
                a sealed vocabulary: two files may use the same category name without the
                slightest relation, because a draw never leaves one file.
            </p>
            <p>
                <strong>A theme's style travels with its words.</strong> Its separator, its
                casing, whether a suffix appears: asking for a theme asks for its format as much
                as its vocabulary. Every name on this site is drawn in the style its own theme
                declares.
            </p>
        </div>

        <Exit
            lead="You have seen the engine and the command that drives it. Both install on their own."
            offers={['Slugger', 'Slugger.Core']}
            extra={{ href: '/themes/', label: 'Every theme slugger ships or carries' }}
        />
    </div>
</section>
